# Bitmagnet Targeted Cleanup Strategy (Staged Torrent Pruning)

> Purpose:
> Gradual, safe removal of low-value torrents and their file metadata
> based on size + age signals to control DB growth.

---
NOTE: KEEP MORE DISK AVAILABLE DURING THIS VACCUM AND REINDEX PHASE


# ⚠️ IMPORTANT NOTES

- These queries ONLY affect `torrent_files`
- They rely on `torrents` metadata for selection
- Run in order (Step 1 → Step 2 → Step 3)
- Repeat cycles if needed for larger cleanup

---

# 🔴 STEP 1 — Remove worst offenders (large + stale torrents)

```sql
DELETE FROM torrent_files
WHERE info_hash IN (
    SELECT t.info_hash
    FROM torrents t
    WHERE t.files_count > 1000
    ORDER BY t.updated_at ASC NULLS FIRST
    LIMIT 50000
);
🟠 STEP 2 — Remove medium + stale torrents
DELETE FROM torrent_files
WHERE info_hash IN (
    SELECT t.info_hash
    FROM torrents t
    WHERE t.files_count BETWEEN 200 AND 1000
    ORDER BY t.updated_at ASC NULLS FIRST
    LIMIT 50000
);
🟡 STEP 3 — Remove oldest remaining torrents
DELETE FROM torrent_files
WHERE info_hash IN (
    SELECT t.info_hash
    FROM torrents t
    ORDER BY t.created_at ASC
    LIMIT 50000
);

🧽 AFTER EACH STEP (IMPORTANT)
VACUUM (ANALYZE) torrent_files;


🧠 FINAL STEP (after all deletions)
VACUUM FULL torrent_files;
REINDEX TABLE torrent_files;




